 "title": "How a Fort Was Built on a 122 m Cliff: Mehrangarh #Shorts",
 "description": "How Mehrangarh in Jodhpur, Rajasthan, sits on a rocky hill about 122 m above the city: founded by Rao Jodha in 1459, walls up to about 36 m high and 21 m wide, a road through seven gates (pols), Jai Pol added by Maharaja Man Singh in 1806, and palaces such as Moti Mahal, Phool Mahal and Sheesh Mahal added by later rulers.\nSource: Mehrangarh Museum Trust.\n\nVisuals and voice are AI-assisted.",
